 search bar -> [Success]\nStep 5: Reason/Think -> [Success] (Result: Reasoning complete)\nStep 6: search bar -> [Success]\nStep 7: Reason/Think -> [Success] (Result: Reasoning complete)\nStep 8: search bar -> [Success]\nStep 9: Reason/Think -> [Success] (Result: Reasoning complete)\nStep 10: open brave -> [Success]\nStep 11: Reason/Think -> [Success] (Result: Reasoning complete)\nStep 12: search bar -> [Success]\nStep 13: Reason/Think -> [Success] (Result: Reasoning complete)\n\n\nRULES:\n1. Analyze the Execution History to understand your progress toward the User's Overall Goal.\n2. If the last step in the history failed, you MUST output a DIFFERENT tool to recover or rethink.\n3. If the Execution History proves that the User's Overall Goal is already fully completed, output exactly: DONE\n4. Otherwise, outline the full remaining sequence of actions required to achieve the goal using ONLY the provided tools.\n5. Output a numbered list of the tool IDs or Names (e.g., '1. open brave\n2. Reason/Think\n3. scroll down').\n6. Only output the tool IDs or Names. Do not include extra text.\n7. If you are not sure what to do next because you need to see the screen, include 'Reason/Think' as a step to wait for the result.\n\nPROPOSED NEXT STEPS:", "output_variable": "plan_output", "response": "1. open brave\n2. Reason/Think\n3. search bar\n4. scroll down"}}
